            <ArticleTitle>Acute leukaemoid reaction following cardiac surgery.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Chronic myelomonocytic leukaemia is an atypical myeloproliferative disorder with a natural history of progression to acute myeloid leukaemia, a complex and poorly understood response by the bone marrow to stress. Cardiac surgery activates many inflammatory cascades and may precipitate a systemic inflammatory response syndrome. We present a case of undiagnosed chronic myelomonocytic leukaemia who developed rapidly fatal multi-organ dysfunction following cardiac surgery due to an acute leukaemoid reaction.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
